{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared vectors for interface-name normalisation.",
    "",
    "The rule is implemented twice - in Go for the collector, which normalises",
    "before a name becomes a metric instance, and in Python for the ingest",
    "worker, which maps whatever arrived onto the name inventory holds. Two",
    "implementations of one rule drift, and the failure is silent: one port",
    "quietly becomes two series again. Both sides test against this file, so a",
    "change to either has to be a change to both.",
    "",
    "'name' is the expanded display form, which also canonicalises the casing",
    "of a name that is already long: an agent reporting 'ethernet1/1' and one",
    "reporting 'Ethernet1/1' should not produce two series.",
    "",
    "'key' is the comparison form: case and non-structural punctuation removed,",
    "but slashes, dots and colons kept, because Ethernet1/1 and Ethernet11 are",
    "different ports. A hyphen is not structural - Port-channel10 keys the same",
    "as Portchannel10."
  ],
